Reference: Access site configuration state from global feed.

**IMPORTANT**: The global feed is a CLIENT-SIDE feature in the SDK.
This tool provides documentation. Config access happens in your client code.

## Site Configuration Events

The global feed broadcasts site-wide configuration changes. Track these to know when:
- Streaming is globally enabled/disabled
- Chat is globally enabled/disabled
- Comments are globally enabled/disabled
- Webhooks are globally enabled/disabled

## Accessing Config State

launchpad-sdk's StreamWebSocketService delivers the config events and keeps the latest value of each
switch: `service.getSiteConfigState()` returns `{ chatEnabled, streamingEnabled, commentsEnabled,
webhooksEnabled, aiModerationEnabled }` (`undefined` for a switch no event has announced since the feed
was joined). The SDK ships no React hooks; in React, read the state in your own component state.

```typescript
import { StreamWebSocketService, getEnvironmentConfig } from '@gala-chain/launchpad-sdk';

const service = new StreamWebSocketService({
  url: getEnvironmentConfig('prod').launchpadBaseUrl,
});

const unsubscribe = service.subscribeToGlobalFeed({
  onSiteConfigChanged: (event) => {
    console.log('Site config changed:', event.key, event.value);
  },
  onStreamGlobalStatus: (data) => {
    console.log('Stream status changed:', data.enabled);
  },
  onStreamChatGlobalStatus: (data) => {
    console.log('Chat status changed:', data.enabled);
  },
  onCommentsGlobalStatus: (data) => {
    console.log('Comments status changed:', data.enabled);
  },
  onWebhooksGlobalStatus: (data) => {
    console.log('Webhooks status changed:', data.enabled);
  },
});
```

## Event Payloads (launchpad-sdk types)

```typescript
interface SiteConfigChangedEvent {   // onSiteConfigChanged
  key: string;
  value: boolean | string;
  timestamp?: number;
}
interface FeatureGlobalStatusEvent { // onStreamGlobalStatus, onStreamChatGlobalStatus, ...
  enabled: boolean;
  timestamp?: number;
}
```

## Events

- **site_config_changed**: Generic config change (includes all flags)
- **stream_global_status**: Streaming enabled/disabled globally
- **chat_global_status**: Chat enabled/disabled globally
- **comments_global_status**: Comments enabled/disabled globally
- **webhooks_global_status**: Webhooks enabled/disabled globally

## Use Cases

1. **Disable UI features**: If streaming is disabled, don't show stream controls
2. **Show status messages**: Inform users when features are globally unavailable
3. **Enable/disable monitoring**: Only set up detailed monitoring if features are enabled
4. **Real-time notifications**: Notify users when features become available/unavailable

